# Core Engineering Rules

Follow `AGENTS.md` and the relevant policies in `.ai/`.

Never:

- duplicate existing functionality
- introduce unnecessary abstractions
- bypass established architecture
- weaken type safety
- ignore errors
- commit secrets
- introduce unexplained dependencies
- modify unrelated files
- leave broken tests
- knowingly introduce quadratic algorithms where a better solution exists

Before writing code:

- inspect existing implementations
- search for reusable utilities
- understand the data flow
- understand ownership of the code
- identify affected tests

Prefer:

- composition
- pure functions
- immutable data where practical
- explicit types
- dependency inversion
- small cohesive modules
- deterministic behavior
- testable business logic

Production source files should normally remain under 200 lines.